  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUMATRAN RHINO PROTECTION IN THE CORE AREA OF THE WESTERN LEUSER ECOSYSTEM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The primary goal of this project is to maintain a zero-poaching rate and a sustained increase in the population of Sumatran rhinos in the western Leuser Ecosystem. The project objectives and activities are as follows: (1) Wildlife Protection Teams (WPT) and post patrol teams equipped with basic gear, such as field clothing, tents, GPS units, and cameras, and providing Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool (SMART) patrol training; (2) Four Wildlife Protection Teams mobilized and reporting on data including rhino signs, report violations to police, produce reports on all WPT patrols; (3) Four patrol posts planned, approved and constructed; and (4) Four post patrols activated and reporting on data.</narrative>
  </description>
